    "fileId": 2138,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Classic lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>More than 50% of the acini in a terminal duct lobular unit are filled and expanded by loosely cohesive monomorphic cells with scant cytoplasm and small uniform nuclei.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2138.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2138.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33285,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2139,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ is characterized by a solid proliferation of dyshesive cells, similar to classic lobular carcinoma in situ, but with marked nuclear pleomorphism equivalent to high-grade ductal carcinoma in situ.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2139.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2139.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33286,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2140,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ lacks membranous E-cadherin expression.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2140.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2140.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33287,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2141,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Apocrine pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>A subset of pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ is further categorized as apocrine type, based on large cells with abundant eosinophilic granular cytoplasm and round to oval nuclei containing prominent nucleoli.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2141.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2141.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33288,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2142,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Apocrine pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Pleomorphic lobular carcinoma in situ is often associated with comedonecrosis and calcifications, leading to mammographic detection.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2142.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2142.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33289,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2143,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Florid lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Florid lobular carcinoma in situ has cytological features similar to those of classic lobular carcinoma in situ (type&nbsp;A and/or type&nbsp;B cells) but is distinguished by marked expansion of terminal duct lobular units with little to no intervening stroma between markedly distended acini of involved terminal duct lobular units.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2143.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2143.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33290,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 13,
    "fileId": 2144,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Florid lobular carcinoma in situ</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>In florid lobular carcinoma in situ, the acini or ducts are markedly expanded (filling at least one high-power field, equivalent to &gt;&nbsp;40&ndash;50&nbsp;cells in diameter) and often associated with central necrosis.</p>",
    "source": "Yunn-Yi Chen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/2144.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/32/13/thumb_2144.jpg"
  },
